From fa0b6e54127aec66677b7b3a7b3379e183d845e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:29:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(trace): union set enumerations of set enumerations as
 TLC does

UnionValue.union computes the UNION of a set enumeration of set
enumerations at once: it keeps each element, in the order it holds the
sets, where equals finds no earlier one equal, and holds the result as
an unnormalized set enumeration, which a membership then tests element
by element. The evaluator sorted the union instead, so a failure after
it named other elements than TLC's, and the startup guards declined
every failed startup definition that evaluated a UNION, 112 of which
matched TLC before them in the upstream suite (`PrintT(1 < UNION {{1},
{2}})`). The evaluator now builds the union as TLC does, and declines
only one TLC keeps lazy.
